- Troubleshooting: `docs/06-Guidelines/troubleshooting.md`
- Contribution: `docs/08-Contribution/contributing.md`

## Source-of-Truth Configuration
- API client: `src/shared/utils/api.ts` with base `/api` (Vite proxy targets `https://mwapss.shibari.photo/api/v1`)
- Auth & routing primitives: `src/core/context/*`, `src/core/router/*`
- OAuth utilities: `src/features/integrations/utils/*`

## Coding Standards (React + TypeScript)
- Functional components and hooks only
- React Query for server state; no ad-hoc fetches in components
- Zod for input and payload validation where applicable
- Mantine v8 for UI; maintain consistent theming and accessibility
- Explicit return types for all exported/public functions
- Early returns; avoid deep nesting (>2–3 levels)
- Centralized error handling with user notifications and typed results
- No duplicate utilities/hooks; consolidate under `src/shared`
- Strict TypeScript: no `any`, no unsafe casts; use precise interfaces and types

## Feature Structure (must follow)
- `types/`: public types and interfaces
- `hooks/`: business logic in composable hooks
- `pages/`: UI components and containers
- `index.ts`: explicit, minimal exports

## Security Requirements
- Auth0 PKCE patterns strictly followed; see `docs/05-Security/README.md`
- Protect routes using `ProtectedRoute` and RBAC
- Never expose tokens; always use the configured API client (auth headers via context)
- OAuth flow: PKCE generation client-side, parameters stored with integration, initiate via backend, backend handles callback, then verify status
- Use HTTPS endpoints only; rely on proxy for development routing

## OAuth/PKCE Frontend Rules
- Generate PKCE verifier/challenge (S256) securely; length 43–128, URL-safe
- Store PKCE params in integration metadata before initiation
- Initiate via POST `/api/v1/oauth/tenants/{tenantId}/integrations/{integrationId}/initiate`
- Callback: frontend should land on client route `/oauth/callback` when required for popup flow; backend `/api/v1/oauth/callback` remains authoritative
- After callback processing, verify with GET `/api/v1/tenants/{tenantId}/integrations/{integrationId}`
- Use popup with `postMessage` for UX; include timeout and fallbacks
- Refresh JWT silently before critical API calls when needed

## Performance
- Memoize expensive calculations (`useMemo`, `useCallback`)
- Use stable dependency arrays and derived variables
- Lazy-load large pages and modules where appropriate
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders; keep component trees shallow

## File Hygiene / Repo Hygiene
- Keep `.cursor` config files committed; ignore sessions/cache/tmp
- `.cursor` volatile files to ignore: `workspace.json`, `sessions/`, `cache/`, `tmp/`
- Keep docs links aligned with nn-folder structure
- Do not commit secrets or environment files; follow `.gitignore`

## Prohibited Changes
- Do not modify `vite.config.ts` proxy
- Do not hardcode environment-specific API URLs
- Do not duplicate existing functions, types, or hooks
- Do not weaken TypeScript strictness or bypass lint rules

## AI Assistance Guidelines (Cursor)
- Reference docs before edits; cite exact file paths when relevant
- Prefer minimal, targeted edits over broad refactors
- Maintain existing code style and formatting in touched files
- When editing code:
  - Add required imports explicitly
  - Maintain type safety and explicit return types
  - Handle errors with user notifications and typed results
  - Keep logic in hooks; keep components lean
- After edits, ensure no linter or TypeScript errors

## Commit & Review Standards
- Conventional commit messages preferred
- Group related changes; avoid mixing unrelated edits
- Reflect documentation updates when changing behavior

## Quick Checklist (before submitting changes)
- Linked docs read and followed (see Documentation Map)
- Patterns reused from `src/features/*` and `src/shared/*`
- TypeScript strict compliance (no `any`, no unsafe casts)
- API calls via `src/shared/utils/api.ts` only
- Security rules enforced (Auth0 PKCE, RBAC, route protection)
- Performance considerations applied (memoization, lazy load)
- UI consistent with Mantine v8 and accessibility guidelines
- Docs links updated (nn-folder structure)

